# Unblessed: Session observation (#438); first blessing awaits human review.
# `:trace` and `:fuel` (session-observation.md): trace rows follow a Host
# call's ordinary output, and Fuel rows follow them. A Command Call shares
# its Entry's Run, so only dispatched Runs are traced. A Fuel Measurement
# follows its Entry's detached sends and error Handler, stays pending while
# any of them waits, and keeps its spent Fuel when a Reload discards work.
> :clock virtual 2026-09-30T10:00:00Z
> on greet name
|   say "hi " & name
| end greet
> on move x to y
|   say x + y
| end move
> on nap
|   wait 5 s
|   say "woke"
| end nap
> on boom
|   return 1 / 0
| end boom
> on error e
|   say "caught " & the code of e
| end error
> :trace nap
> :trace greet
> :trace move:to:
> :trace error
> :trace greet
> :trace
trace "error"
trace "greet"
trace "move:to:"
trace "nap"
> :trace bad name
! bad arguments
> :untrace move:
! bad arguments
> greet "Ann"
hi Ann
> send greet with "Bo" to session
[session/r3] hi Bo
trace start {script: "session", run: "session/r3", selector: "greet", args: ["Bo"]}
trace end {script: "session", run: "session/r3", selector: "greet", outcome: "completed", result: nothing}
> send to session: move 1 to 2
[session/r5] 3
trace start {script: "session", run: "session/r5", selector: "move:to:", args: [1, 2]}
trace end {script: "session", run: "session/r5", selector: "move:to:", outcome: "completed", result: nothing}
